==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} A [[holler]] back; a reply.
# {{lb|en|informal}} An echo of voices, much like the response of a crowd to a [[cheerleader]].
# {{lb|en|informal|uncountable}} [[feedback|Feedback]].

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} To reply.
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|title=This Life Isn't Perfect Holla|author=Sandra Foy|year=2008|ISBN=1585715859|passage=“Earth to Kimi, '''holla back''',” Yvonne taunts after I miss another easy serve.}}
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|title=Essential Encouragement: Poetry with a Purpose|author=Vanessa Clark|year=2012|page=71|ISBN=1477263519|passage=When depression or breakdown is hollerin' at you . . . . '''holla back'''. When temptation or weakness is hollerin' at you . . . . '''holla back'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|title=Sun-Kissed|author=Melissa de la Cruz|year=2013|page=80|ISBN=1442474165|passage=“'''Holla back''', girl! Where are you?” Mara asked, feeling a flush of happiness at hearing Eliza's throaty voice.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} To make or respond to romantic or sexual overtures.
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|title=Qvmagazine - Volume 6, Issues 1-2|year=2003|passage=I have a goatee, moustache, and medium thick eyebrows. Here to meet some cool peeps so '''Holla back''' at your Boy.}}
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|title=Poems by E Presents from the Light to the Darkness and Back to Life|author=Eldon M. Thomas|year=2007|page=1434324362|passage=So '''holla back''' at me beautiful sista girl Let this chocolate lover into your chocolate world}}
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|title=Women: The New Doggs|author=Ian J. Findlay & Saunie Brown|year=2009|ISBN=1469116006|passage=“Anyway,” She grabbed his dick through his black silk boxers, “I'll '''holla back''' big man."}}
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|title=I Am Not the Father: Narratives of Men Falsely Accused of Paternity|author=M. L. Matthews|year=2010|page=78|ISBN=1426937032|passage=You don't break up with me then try to '''holla back''' at me. So that's when she called asking if we can have a sexual type of relationship.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} To contact again at a later time.
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|title=The Reading: What You Knew You Didn't Know|author=Sexton Classford|year=2006|page=30|ISBN=0595401139|passage='''Holla back''' when you get outta church. just got ya message, i saw it when it popped up.}}
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|title=Climbing Trees and Hiding in the Bushes|author=Adriana Jai Wynn-Yeldell|year=2009|page=338|ISBN=1438989172|passage=I feel ya man, go set her straight on Cally and '''holla back''' at me.}}
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|title=If I Knew Back Then What I Know Now|author=Tamika Davis|year=2010|page=39|ISBN=0557375444|passage=“Alright I'll do that and '''holla back''' on Monday with the 411. Talk to you soon cuz."}}
#* {{quote-book|lang=en|title=Back To Me|author=Earl Sewell|year=2012|ISBN=1460885430|passage=I'll '''holla back''' at you later, he wrote, ending our conversation.}}